---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '@fontsource-variable/figtree';
import '@fontsource/hind-siliguri';
import '@fontsource/hind-siliguri/700.css';
import '@fontsource-variable/hanken-grotesk';
import '@fontsource-variable/noto-sans-bengali';
const check = `<svg width="9" height="9" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 6.5l2.6 2.6L10 3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>`;
---
<Base title="LofiCare variants board" description="Pick one card per row. Nothing on this page ships.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="intro">
      <img src="/brand/loficare-mark.png" alt="" width="56" height="56" />
      <h1>Variants board</h1>
      <p>One card per row. Your picks collect in the bar at the bottom; copy them and paste them back. Everything here uses the real tokens, the candidate fonts and the brief's copy at small scale. This page is deleted before launch.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="pick" data-key="world">
      <h2>1. The visual world</h2>
      <p>impeccable's roll assigned the third direction of a list grounded in a facility owner's daily world. The other rows are structures that live inside whichever world you choose.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="W-A">
          <div class="mini ink">
            <div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between;align-items:center"><img class="marklet" src="/brand/loficare-mark.png" alt="" /><span class="m">EN · বাংলা</span></div>
            <p class="t" style="margin:6px 0 4px;max-width:20ch">Run your whole facility on one platform, built for Bangladesh.</p>
            <div class="board"><span class="m" style="color:var(--mist-on-ink)">NOW SERVING</span><div class="row" style="align-items:baseline;gap:8px"><span class="n">12</span><span>Dr. Rahman · Room 3</span></div><div class="row" style="gap:10px;margin-top:3px"><span>13</span><span>14</span><span>15</span><span class="m">next</span></div></div>
            <div class="row" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="b">Book a demo</span><span class="b o">Start free with Appointments</span></div>
          </div>
          <h3>A. The queue board <small>Assigned by the roll</small></h3>
          <p>The waiting-room serial display every owner watches all day: ink ground, aqua digits, one row stepping at a time, numbers set as facts. The brand aqua is the color those boards already glow. Motion is a step, an overshoot, a settle, never a fade.</p>
          <p class="risk">Risk: it can read as a patient screen if the copy does not keep the owner in the seat.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose W-A</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="W-B">
          <div class="mini">
            <p class="t" style="max-width:22ch">One record, from the front desk to the report.</p>
            <div class="col" style="margin-top:6px;gap:0">
              <div class="row hair" style="padding:3px 0;color:var(--slate)"><span style="flex:1">Reg</span><span style="flex:1">Sample</span><span style="flex:1">Result</span><span style="flex:1">Bill</span><span style="flex:1">Referrer</span></div>
              <div class="row hair" style="padding:3px 0"><span style="flex:1">A-1042</span><span style="flex:1">BC 88213</span><span style="flex:1"><span class="stamp">VERIFIED</span></span><span style="flex:1">1,850</span><span style="flex:1">Dr. Sultana</span></div>
              <div class="row hair" style="padding:3px 0;color:var(--slate)"><span style="flex:1">A-1043</span><span style="flex:1">BC 88214</span><span style="flex:1">entering</span><span style="flex:1">2,300</span><span style="flex:1">walk-in</span></div>
              <div class="row hair" style="padding:3px 0;color:var(--slate)"><span style="flex:1">A-1044</span><span style="flex:1">collected</span><span style="flex:1"></span><span style="flex:1"></span><span style="flex:1">Dr. Karim</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px"><span class="b">Book a demo</span></div>
          </div>
          <h3>B. The one record <small>Impeccable's pick</small></h3>
          <p>My own first choice: the registration ledger, the ruled book every counter keeps, digitized. Hairline rows, one connected line per patient across every module, the page itself a ledger that fills as you scroll.</p>
          <p class="risk">Risk: ruled hairline pages are a familiar editorial move; it only feels like ours if the row mechanic carries the modules.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose W-B</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card quiet" data-code="W-C">
          <div class="mini">
            <div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between"><span style="font-weight:800;color:var(--teal-700)">LofiCare</span><span class="b">Book a demo</span></div>
            <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:8px"><div><p class="t">The complete hospital and diagnostic centre platform.</p><p class="m" style="margin-top:3px">Appointments live today, free to start.</p></div><div class="frame" style="height:52px"></div></div>
            <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px"><div class="tile" style="flex:1">Diagnostics</div><div class="tile" style="flex:1">Hospitals</div><div class="tile" style="flex:1">Doctors</div></div>
          </div>
          <h3>C. Clean clinical SaaS, played straight <small>The category standard</small></h3>
          <p>White page, teal headings, product panel right, feature rows, pricing, FAQ. The safe door. If you take it, name two products it should sit beside and we hold their craft level.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose W-C</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="theme">
      <h2>2. Theme</h2>
      <p>Decision D1. Where the ink lives.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="T-A">
          <div class="mini strips"><div class="s ink">hero</div><div class="s">doors · trust · problem</div><div class="s alt">platform</div><div class="s">diagnostics · hospitals</div><div class="s alt">appointments · doctors</div><div class="s">patients · data · cohorts · pricing · faq</div><div class="s ink">demo · footer</div></div>
          <h3>A. Light page, two mirrored ink bands <small>PM default</small></h3>
          <p>Daylight offices and phones outdoors read light pages better. The aqua mark still gets its dark ground twice: the opening and the close.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose T-A</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="T-B">
          <div class="mini strips"><div class="s ink">hero</div><div class="s ink2">doors · trust · problem</div><div class="s ink">platform</div><div class="s ink2">diagnostics · hospitals</div><div class="s ink">appointments · doctors</div><div class="s ink2">patients · data · cohorts · pricing · faq</div><div class="s ink">demo · footer</div></div>
          <h3>B. Ink throughout</h3>
          <p>The lockup's own ground on every section, lifted and dropped between ink 950 and ink 900. Stronger brand, harder on long reading and on cheap screens in sunlight.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose T-B</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="hero">
      <h2>3. Hero</h2>
      <p>All three keep the pinned moment: the eighteen module tiles assemble into the mark, the appointment cross lit, the rest honestly unlit. They differ in what the copy sits beside.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="H-1">
          <div class="mini ink">
            <div class="grid2" style="height:100%;gap:8px">
              <div class="col" style="justify-content:center"><p class="t">Run your whole facility on one platform, built for Bangladesh.</p><p class="m" style="margin-top:4px">One connected system for diagnostic centres and hospitals. Online appointments are live today and free to start.</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="b">Book a demo</span><span class="b o">Start free</span></div></div>
              <div class="scene"><span class="sq" style="left:6%;top:10%"></span><span class="sq" style="left:22%;top:70%"></span><span class="sq" style="left:70%;top:8%"></span><span class="sq" style="left:80%;top:78%"></span><span class="sq" style="left:12%;top:42%"></span><img src="/brand/loficare-mark.png" alt="" style="position:absolute;inset:18%;width:64%;height:64%;object-fit:contain" /></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <h3>1. Split, mark assembling right</h3>
          <p>Copy left, the assembly right. The plainest reading of the brief's platform-first hero. On phones the copy comes first and the assembly sits below it at about half the viewport.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose H-1</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="H-2">
          <div class="mini ink boardbg">
            <div class="col" style="height:100%;justify-content:space-between">
              <div><p class="t" style="max-width:24ch">Run your whole facility on one platform, built for Bangladesh.</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="b">Book a demo</span><span class="b o">Start free</span></div></div>
              <div class="scene" style="position:absolute;right:6%;top:8%;width:38%;height:60%"><span class="sq" style="left:0;top:0"></span><span class="sq" style="left:60%;top:20%"></span><span class="sq" style="left:20%;top:70%"></span><img src="/brand/loficare-mark.png" alt="" style="position:absolute;inset:12%;width:76%;height:76%;object-fit:contain" /></div>
              <div class="board" style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:baseline"><span class="m" style="color:var(--mist-on-ink)">NOW SERVING</span><span class="n">12</span><span>13 · 14 · 15</span><span class="m" style="margin-left:auto;color:var(--mist-on-ink)">10:40</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <h3>2. Board as ground</h3>
          <p>The whole hero is the waiting-room board: a faint cell grid, copy set on it, tiles stepping into the mark inside the grid, a live serial strip along the foot. The most committed reading of world A.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose H-2</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="H-3">
          <div class="mini ink">
            <div class="grid2" style="height:100%;gap:8px">
              <div class="col" style="justify-content:center"><p class="t">Run your whole facility on one platform, built for Bangladesh.</p><p class="m" style="margin-top:4px">Appointments live today, free to start.</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="b">Book a demo</span><span class="b o">Start free</span></div></div>
              <div class="frame col" style="gap:3px;font-size:9px"><div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between;color:var(--slate)"><span>Today · Chamber 2</span><span class="num">10:40</span></div><div class="row tile" style="justify-content:space-between;border-color:var(--green)"><span><b>12</b> Farhana A.</span><span class="badge g">in room</span></div><div class="row tile" style="justify-content:space-between"><span><b>13</b> Md. Shakil</span><span class="m">waiting</span></div><div class="row tile" style="justify-content:space-between"><span><b>14</b> Ruma D.</span><span class="m">confirmed</span></div><div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between;color:var(--slate)"><span>Empty chairs today</span><span class="num">0</span></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <h3>3. The live day</h3>
          <p>Copy left, the actual appointment module right as a working component stepping through a doctor's morning with sample data. The assembly moves down to the platform section. Proves the live module in the first viewport.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose H-3</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="doors">
      <h2>4. The three doors</h2>
      <p>Directly under the hero. Facility first, doctor second, patient quiet.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="D-1">
          <div class="mini"><div class="grid3" style="height:100%"><div class="tile col" style="justify-content:space-between"><div><p class="t">Diagnostic centre or hospital?</p><p class="m">One platform for the whole facility.</p></div><span class="b">Book a demo</span></div><div class="tile col" style="justify-content:space-between"><p class="t" style="font-size:11px">Independent doctor?</p><span class="b o" style="color:var(--teal-700)">Start free</span></div><div class="col" style="justify-content:space-between;padding:4px"><p class="m">Patient?</p><a class="m" style="color:var(--teal-700);text-decoration:underline">Find your doctor</a></div></div></div>
          <h3>1. Stepped tiles</h3>
          <p>Widths by priority: the facility tile widest, the doctor medium, the patient a quiet text link. Never three equal cards.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose D-1</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="D-2">
          <div class="mini ink"><div class="col" style="gap:5px;height:100%;justify-content:center"><div class="row tile" style="justify-content:space-between;border-color:var(--aqua-400)"><span><b class="aqua">01</b> Diagnostic centre or hospital</span><span class="b">Book a demo</span></div><div class="row tile" style="justify-content:space-between"><span><b>02</b> Independent doctor</span><span class="b o">Start free</span></div><div class="row tile" style="justify-content:space-between;color:var(--mist-on-ink)"><span><b>03</b> Patient</span><span>Find your doctor</span></div></div></div>
          <h3>2. Board rows</h3>
          <p>Three destinations on the board, the facility row lit. Extends the hero's grammar one screen further, then the page goes light.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose D-2</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="D-3">
          <div class="mini"><div class="row" style="border:1px solid var(--mist);border-radius:99px;padding:2px;width:max-content"><span class="b" style="border-radius:99px">I run a facility</span><span style="padding:3px 7px">I am a doctor</span><span style="padding:3px 7px">I am a patient</span></div><div class="tile" style="margin-top:8px"><p class="t">Run the whole facility, not one desk.</p><p class="m" style="margin:3px 0 6px">Referrer earnings, samples, results, reports, billing, on one record.</p><span class="b">Book a demo</span></div></div>
          <h3>3. Segmented switch</h3>
          <p>One control, three panels. Interactive and compact on phones, but it hides two doors behind a tap and asks the visitor to self-identify before reading.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose D-3</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="trust">
      <h2>5. Trust line</h2>
      <p>One honest signal, no logos.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="R-1">
          <div class="mini" style="background:var(--wash-50);display:grid;place-items:center"><p class="t" style="text-align:center;font-size:13px">Built in Bangladesh. Your patients' data stays in Bangladesh.</p></div>
          <h3>1. One statement strip</h3>
          <p>A single line on wash, full width. Nothing to scan, nothing to doubt.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose R-1</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="R-2">
          <div class="mini" style="background:var(--wash-50);display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center"><div><p class="t bn" style="font-size:13px">বাংলাদেশে তৈরি। আপনার রোগীদের তথ্য বাংলাদেশেই থাকে।</p><p class="m" style="margin-top:4px">Built in Bangladesh. Your patients' data stays in Bangladesh.</p></div></div>
          <h3>2. Bangla first, English under</h3>
          <p>The one line that is bilingual on both routes, Bangla leading. Says "built here" in the language itself.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose R-2</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="problem">
      <h2>6. The problem</h2>
      <p>"A facility runs on too many disconnected systems." Both readers must feel it.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="P-1">
          <div class="mini"><p class="t">A facility runs on too many disconnected systems.</p><div class="grid2" style="margin-top:6px"><div class="m"><b style="color:var(--ink-950)">The facility.</b> Registration in one book, samples on slips, results retyped, commissions in a notebook.</div><div class="m"><b style="color:var(--ink-950)">The chamber.</b> The booking line busy, the serial in one assistant's head, the room asking whose turn.</div></div><svg viewBox="0 0 200 30" style="width:100%;height:26px;margin-top:6px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 25 C40 25 40 5 80 5 M5 5 C40 5 40 25 80 25 M80 15 H120" stroke="var(--teal-600)" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/><rect x="120" y="8" width="70" height="14" rx="3" fill="var(--aqua-400)"/></svg></div>
          <h3>1. Two columns and a joining line</h3>
          <p>Headline, the two pains side by side, one animated line drawing where the strands meet. Calm, as the brief asks.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose P-1</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="P-2">
          <div class="mini" style="position:relative"><p class="t">Too many disconnected systems.</p><span class="slip" style="left:6%;top:38%;transform:rotate(-6deg)">Registration book</span><span class="slip" style="left:40%;top:30%;transform:rotate(4deg)">Sample slip</span><span class="slip" style="left:62%;top:52%;transform:rotate(-3deg)">Result, retyped</span><span class="slip" style="left:14%;top:66%;transform:rotate(5deg)">Commission notebook</span><span class="slip" style="left:58%;top:78%;transform:rotate(-8deg)">Report, late</span></div>
          <h3>2. Scattered slips align</h3>
          <p>The paper of the current workflow, thrown across the section, straightening into one row as you scroll. Typographic, no illustration to draw.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose P-2</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="P-3">
          <div class="mini"><div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between;align-items:center"><p class="t">Before and after</p><span class="row" style="border:1px solid var(--mist);border-radius:99px;padding:2px"><span style="padding:1px 6px">Today</span><span class="b" style="border-radius:99px">LofiCare</span></span></div><div class="grid2" style="margin-top:6px"><div class="tile" style="opacity:.55"><div class="m">reg book</div><div class="m">sample slips</div><div class="m">notebook</div><div class="m">retyped result</div></div><div class="tile" style="border-color:var(--green)"><div>one record</div><div>barcoded sample</div><div>referrer statement</div><div>report released</div></div></div></div>
          <h3>3. Before and after switch</h3>
          <p>A two-state control the visitor flips. Shows the fix in the same breath as the pain, but it spends the section's calm on an interaction.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose P-3</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="platform">
      <h2>7. The 18 modules</h2>
      <p>This section earns the "complete platform" claim. Only the appointment chip is Available now.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="G-1">
          <div class="mini"><div class="row" style="gap:8px"><b style="width:52px;color:var(--teal-700)">Core</b><div><span class="chip">Facility and access</span><span class="chip">Patient registry</span><span class="chip">Doctor and referrer</span><span class="chip on">Appointments</span><span class="chip">Billing</span><span class="chip">Credit accounts</span></div></div><div class="row hair" style="gap:8px;padding-top:4px;margin-top:4px"><b style="width:52px;color:var(--teal-700)">Diagnostics</b><div><span class="chip">Samples and barcode</span><span class="chip">Verification and QC</span><span class="chip">Imaging</span><span class="chip">Report release</span></div></div><div class="row hair" style="gap:8px;padding-top:4px;margin-top:4px"><b style="width:52px;color:var(--teal-700)">Hospital</b><div><span class="chip">Inpatient, ward, OT</span><span class="chip">Pharmacy</span><span class="chip">Workforce</span></div></div></div>
          <h3>1. Tier rows with chips</h3>
          <p>Eight tier rows, chips inside, tier labels stick on desktop. Reads as a system map. Compact on phones.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose G-1</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="G-2">
          <div class="mini"><div class="bento"><div class="tile" style="grid-area:a"><b>Core</b><div><span class="chip on">Appointments</span><span class="chip">Registry</span><span class="chip">Billing</span><span class="chip">Referrers</span><span class="chip">Credit</span></div></div><div class="tile" style="grid-area:b"><b>Diagnostics</b><div><span class="chip">Samples</span><span class="chip">QC</span><span class="chip">Imaging</span><span class="chip">Reports</span></div></div><div class="tile" style="grid-area:c"><b>Hospital</b></div><div class="tile" style="grid-area:d"><b>Supply</b></div><div class="tile" style="grid-area:e"><b>Clinical</b></div><div class="tile" style="grid-area:f"><b>Insight</b></div></div></div>
          <h3>2. Bento by tier</h3>
          <p>Tiles sized by module count: Core largest, Diagnostics next, the rest small. Exactly eight cells, no blanks. Needs real visual variation in two or three cells.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose G-2</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="G-3">
          <div class="mini ink" style="display:grid;place-items:center"><div style="position:relative;width:120px;height:120px"><img src="/brand/loficare-mark.png" alt="" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;opacity:.25" /><span class="chip" style="position:absolute;left:34%;top:38%;border-color:var(--green);color:var(--aqua-200)">Appointments</span><span class="chip" style="position:absolute;left:52%;top:4%;color:var(--mist-on-ink)">Imaging</span><span class="chip" style="position:absolute;left:2%;top:50%;color:var(--mist-on-ink)">Billing</span><span class="chip" style="position:absolute;left:58%;top:70%;color:var(--mist-on-ink)">Pharmacy</span><span class="chip" style="position:absolute;left:6%;top:80%;color:var(--mist-on-ink)">Registry</span><span class="chip" style="position:absolute;left:66%;top:36%;color:var(--mist-on-ink)">Reports</span></div></div>
          <h3>3. The exploded mark</h3>
          <p>The chips laid in the mark's silhouette, appointments at the cross. Closes the loop with the hero, but eighteen labels in a shape is hard to read on a phone and needs a list fallback.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose G-3</button>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pick" data-key="diagnostics">
      <h2>8. For diagnostic centres</h2>
      <p>"Know what every referrer earns. Get reports out faster." The sharpest wedge.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card" data-code="X-1">
          <div class="mini"><p class="t">Know what every referrer earns. Get reports out faster.</p><div class="row" style="margin-top:8px;align-items:center;gap:0"><span class="step">Collect</span><span class="ln"></span><span class="step">Barcode</span><span class="ln"></span><span class="step">Verify</span><span class="ln"></span><span class="step">Release</span><span class="ln"></span><span class="step">Deliver</span></div><div class="tile row" style="margin-top:8px;justify-content:space-between"><span>Dr. Sultana · 42 referrals · Sept</span><span class="num">18,900</span><span class="badge m">Early access</span></div></div>
          <h3>1. Flow stepper plus referrer statement</h3>
          <p>The sample's five stations in a row, a referrer statement row beneath, both labelled Early access. Reads at a glance on desktop; stacks on phones.</p>
          <button class="choose" type="button">Choose X-1</button>
        </article>
        <article class="card" data-code="X-2">
